 ],
 "literal": "If we said, 'If you go, the journey will be difficult,' saying so / in the desert, on the beautiful forked branch of the ōmai tree, perched / the clear call, full of loneliness, of the kite separated from its flock / becomes a comforting companion to the distressed people who travel through the desert. / Beside the rocky mountain, on the ancient, narrow path frequented by travelers, / imprinting her beautiful feet, she crossed over and / went, so we heard from many well-wishers.",
 "translation": "If we had spoken, saying, 'If you go, the journey will be difficult,' he would have stayed. But now, we have heard from many well-wishers that she has crossed over, imprinting her beautiful feet on the ancient, narrow path frequented by travelers beside the rocky mountain, where the clear, lonely call of a kite separated from its flock, perched on the beautiful forked branch of an ōmai tree in the desert, becomes a comforting companion to the distressed travelers.",
 "modern": "‘நீங்கள் சென்றால் பயணம் கடினமாக இருக்கும்’ என்று நாம் தடுத்திருந்தால் அவர் சென்றிருக்க மாட்டார். ஆனால், பாலைவனத்து ஓமை மரத்தின் அழகிய கிளையில் அமர்ந்திருக்கும், தன் கூட்டத்தைப் பிரிந்த பருந்தின் தனிமை நிறைந்த தெளிவான குரலானது, அங்குச் செல்லும் துயருற்ற மக்களுக்குத் துணையாக இருக்கும் என்று கூறுவர். அத்தகைய கல் மலைக்கு அருகில் உள்ள, மக்கள் பண்டுதொட்டு நடந்து பழகிய குறுகிய பாதையில், அவளுடைய மெல்லிய பாதங்கள் பதியுமாறு அவள் கடந்து சென்றுவிட்டாள் என்று அன்புடைய பலர் கூற நாம் கேட்டோம்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is set in the pālai (desert) landscape, depicting the theme of separation. The speaker is the foster-mother of the heroine, who has eloped with her lover. She laments that if she had only spoken up and warned them of the difficulties of the journey, they might not have gone. Now, travelers and well-wishers returning from the desert path have informed her that they saw the young heroine walking on the harsh, narrow mountain path, her tender feet leaving prints on the stones. The image of the lonely kite calling from the dry ōmai tree reflects the desolate atmosphere of the desert, yet its cry serves as a strange companion to the weary travelers, mirroring the heroine's own journey through hardship with her beloved.",
